//@version=6

// =============================================================================
// BTC PRO ANALYSIS ENGINE
// PHASE A (Data Gate) + PHASE B (Market Regime) + PHASE C (Structure + Zones +
// Fibonacci + Breakout/Retest FSM) + PHASE D (Price Action + Momentum +
// Participation) — built incrementally, one module at a time, each
// confirmed working before the next is added (Madde 122).
//
// MODULES INCLUDED SO FAR:
//   1. DATA GATE + SYMBOL VALIDATION + STATE MACHINE SKELETON (Madde 7, 1, 8, 55)
//      — confirmed working by user on OKX:BTCUSDT and TVC:DEU40.
//   2. MARKET REGIME + VOLATILITY REGIME + REGIME CONFIDENCE (Madde 9, 10, 11)
//      — confirmed working by user (TRANSITION/LOW confidence in a chop zone;
//      persistence/hysteresis held through Replay without flip-flopping).
//   3. MARKET STRUCTURE — CENTRAL CONFIRMED-SWING FUNCTION + HH/HL/LH/LL +
//      BOS/CHoCH (Madde 14, 61) — confirmed working by user, including that
//      swing markers only appear ~pivotRight bars after the fact (KNOWN_TIME
//      vs SWING_TIME, Madde 14) and are stable across reload/replay (no repaint).
//   4. SUPPORT/RESISTANCE ZONE ENGINE + CLUSTERING (Madde 15, 16) — confirmed
//      working by user (also caught and fixed an empty-array crash, v0.4.1).
//   5. FIBONACCI ENGINE (Madde 17) — confirmed working by user (levels
//      consistent with LAST SWING HIGH/LOW).
//   6. BREAKOUT / RETEST STATE MACHINE (Madde 20-21) — last remaining item in
//      the Phase C roadmap (Madde 121). Reuses the SAME crossedAboveLastHigh/
//      crossedBelowLastLow break-of-level signals already computed for
//      Structure's BOS/CHoCH (no new level logic invented, Madde 111). States:
//      PRE_BREAKOUT -> BREAKOUT_CANDIDATE -> CONFIRMED_BREAKOUT (displacement
//      >= N x ATR) -> RETEST_PENDING (price returns near the level) ->
//      RETEST_ACCEPTED/ENTRY, or the failure path BREAKOUT_CANDIDATE/
//      CONFIRMED_BREAKOUT/RETEST_PENDING -> FAILED_BREAKOUT ->
//      REVERSAL_CANDIDATE, or STALE if a stage times out (Madde 20). Per
//      Madde 21, "breakout quality" factors that belong to Participation/
//      Momentum (volume, momentum confirmation) are NOT fabricated here since
//      those modules don't exist yet — this FSM only uses STRUCTURE-family
//      evidence (price vs. level). Reaching the ENTRY state is a structural
//      label, NOT a trading signal — no alert/decision logic is wired to it.
//
//   Also, per user request: the temporary diagnostics table now has a
//   COMPACT/FULL toggle (Diagnostics Detail input) and smaller text
//   (text_size=tiny everywhere), since it was growing every module and risked
//   becoming unusable on small screens before the real Madde 114 panel exists.
//
//   7. PRICE ACTION ENGINE (Madde 22) — first item of Phase D (Confirmation).
//      Mathematical, not a pattern zoo: BODY/RANGE, WICK/BODY, CLOSE
//      LOCATION, RANGE/ATR are the primitives (Madde 22's own instruction),
//      and only a minimal named-pattern set is derived from them: bullish/
//      bearish engulfing, hammer/shooting-star shape, upper/lower rejection
//      wick, inside/outside bar, strong close up/down. "Breakout candle
//      quality" was intentionally NOT rebuilt as a separate metric — it
//      would just reuse these same body/wick/range primitives that the
//      Breakout FSM's displacement check already covers structurally
//      (Madde 111: don't rebuild redundant concepts). Snapshotted on
//      confirmed bars only (Madde 33-34), tagged EvidenceFamily.TRIGGER
//      (Madde 64 lists "rejection", "reclaim", "close confirmation" as
//      trigger examples — Price Action patterns here are that same kind of
//      evidence, not a new family). Price Action is explicitly NOT an entry
//      by itself (Madde 22): no Setup/Trigger/Decision engine consumes it yet.
//
//   8. MOMENTUM ENGINE (Madde 23) — second item of Phase D. Uses RSI + MACD
//      histogram only, NOT also Stochastic/CCI as Madde 23 casually lists —
//      those would be highly redundant with RSI in the same MOMENTUM family
//      (Madde 6 double-counting ban). The goal is a STATE label
//      (ACCELERATING/DECELERATING/RECOVERING/WEAKENING/NEUTRAL), never "RSI
//      30 = LONG" (Madde 23 explicit prohibition, honored: RSI/MACD values
//      never feed any direction/entry logic here, only the state label).
//      Divergence detection reuses the SAME central confirmed-swing function
//      (Madde 14 v3.1 EK) — RSI is snapshotted at each confirmed swing bar
//      (inside Structure's existing swing-registration blocks, a small
//      addition, not a rewrite) and compared HH-vs-lower-RSI /
//      LL-vs-higher-RSI. Reported as DIVERGENCE DETECTED, never as a
//      guaranteed reversal (Madde 23). Tagged EvidenceFamily.MOMENTUM.
//
//   9. PARTICIPATION ENGINE (Madde 24) — third and last Phase D item, so
//      Phase D is now complete per the Madde 121 roadmap. Uses RVOL
//      (volume / N-bar average) + OBV slope alignment with price direction
//      only, NOT every volume-flavored indicator Madde 24 casually lists —
//      OBV, price-volume alignment and breakout volume all measure closely
//      related information, so piling them on would double-count within this
//      one PARTICIPATION family (Madde 6). VWAP is a FIXED N-bar ROLLING
//      average (sum(close*volume)/sum(volume) over N bars via ta.sma ratio),
//      deliberately NOT TradingView's session-anchored ta.vwap — Madde 24
//      explicitly warns that BTC is 24/7, so no exchange "session open"
//      concept is assumed (consistent with Madde 1/107's BIST-session ban).
//      STATE label (NORMAL/EXPANDING/CONTRACTING/CONFIRMING/DIVERGING) from
//      RVOL magnitude x OBV/price alignment. Tagged
//      EvidenceFamily.PARTICIPATION. BACKLOG (per user, not built): zone
//      "polarity flip" (a broken resistance zone re-evaluated as a support
//      candidate) — deliberately not in Madde 15-16's spec, revisit when
//      Location/Zone Quality (Madde 62-63) or the Setup Classifier is built,
//      where its actual effect can be measured (Madde 111).
//
//  10. MTF REFINEMENT (Madde 28-32) — first item of Phase E (Context).
//      Relative Strength (Madde 27's OTHER Phase E item) is deliberately NOT
//      built this turn (Madde 122: one module per turn) — it is explicitly
//      "not mandatory for a BTC-only system" per Madde 27, and needs a user
//      decision on which benchmark to use, so it is deferred to its own
//      turn. This module requests exactly ONE higher timeframe (HTF), chosen
//      via a simple, explainable chart-TF -> HTF map (Madde 28's default
//      role table, collapsed to "one level up" from the current chart:
//      <=15m->1H, <=1H->4H, <=4H->1D, >=1D->N/A, no higher default role) or
//      a MANUAL override input; if the manual HTF is not actually higher
//      than the chart TF, MTF is reported UNAVAILABLE rather than showing
//      fabricated data (Madde 139/140). Exactly ONE request.security() call
//      is used, bundling THREE values as a single tuple (HTF close, HTF EMA,
//      HTF EMA N-bars-earlier for slope) — Madde 110's "prefer one tuple
//      request over several separate calls" — so this module costs exactly
//      ONE request.*() slot (0/40 -> 1/40, see REQUEST BUDGET diagnostics
//      row). Non-repainting per Madde 29: EVERY value inside the tuple is
//      offset with `[1]` (the slope value with `[lookback+1]`) AND the call
//      uses `lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on` — the official TradingView
//      non-repainting HTF pattern (confirmed HTF bar data only, one HTF bar
//      of lag accepted on purpose). Bare `lookahead_on` without offsetting
//      the expression is explicitly forbidden by Madde 29 and is NOT used
//      anywhere in this script. Produces an HTF_BIAS (BULLISH/BEARISH/
//      NEUTRAL, from simple HTF close-vs-EMA + EMA-slope agreement, Madde 10
//      — no re-derivation of the full Regime/Structure engines on the HTF,
//      which would be fragile/expensive to evaluate via request.security)
//      and an MTF_AGREEMENT versus the chart's OWN structureBias (AGREE/
//      CONFLICT/NEUTRAL/UNAVAILABLE). Tagged EvidenceFamily.MTF. Per Madde
//      31, MTF agreement/conflict here is CONTEXT ONLY — it does NOT
//      produce any automatic LONG/SHORT, and no timeframe gets its own
//      independent score (no scoring engine exists yet regardless).
//
//      Phase E is now COMPLETE. Relative Strength (Madde 27, Phase E's
//      other item) was explicitly SKIPPED by user decision, not merely
//      postponed: Madde 27 itself says RS is not mandatory for a BTC-only
//      system, and rather than guess a benchmark the user was asked to pick
//      one (BTC Dominance / BTC-vs-TOTAL2 / macro DXY-SPX / skip) and chose
//      to skip it and move straight to Phase F. No RS code, enum, or
//      diagnostics row exists in this script — RS is simply absent, not
//      faked as a permanent "UNAVAILABLE" placeholder (Madde 139/140: don't
//      build UI for a feature that was declined, that would itself be a
//      kind of fake signal of completeness).
//
//  11. RISK ENGINE (Madde 44-49) — first item of Phase F (Decision). A
//      DIAGNOSTIC CALCULATOR only, exactly like Fibonacci/Zone — it is NOT
//      wired to any entry/trade signal because no Setup Classifier exists
//      yet (Madde 18-19, still not built) to define what a live "setup"
//      even is. Instead of building unused generic formulas with no
//      consumer, or fabricating a fake live signal, this computes what the
//      stop/target/R:R/position size WOULD be for a structural LONG and a
//      structural SHORT idea anchored on price right now, reusing the
//      SAME nearest-zone lookups the Zone module already computed
//      (nearestResIdx/nearestSupIdx, Madde 111 — no new zone search).
//      Stop hierarchy (Madde 45): STRUCTURAL INVALIDATION (nearest opposing
//      zone edge, or the last confirmed swing if no zone exists yet) +
//      ATR BUFFER, then checked against MAX ACCEPTABLE STOP DISTANCE — a
//      stop is never a "random %". If no structural level exists at all,
//      the result is explicitly "NO STRUCTURAL STOP", never a fabricated
//      number (Madde 45: "mantıklı stop yoksa NO TRADE", Madde 139/140).
//      Target (Madde 46) is the near edge of the opposing zone, not a blind
//      "entry + 2 ATR" (Madde 46 explicit prohibition). R:R (Madde 47) is
//      compared against a minimum (default 1.5, stated in Madde 47 itself
//      as a starting hypothesis to validate later, NOT to optimize now,
//      Madde 10/47). Position sizing (Madde 48): Risk Amount = Equity x
//      Risk%, Position Size = Risk Amount / Stop Distance; leverage
//      defaults to 1.0 (spot/no leverage) and is never assumed higher
//      without the user explicitly setting it (Madde 48 explicit rule).
//      Tagged EvidenceFamily.RISK. Shown for BOTH long and short structural
//      ideas simultaneously (Madde 50 long/short symmetry audit) — neither
//      side is privileged.
//
//  12. SETUP CLASSIFIER (Madde 18-19) — "setup-specific decision rules",
//      second item of Phase F, per user decision (Position Sizing's own
//      formula already exists inside the Risk Engine above and works;
//      Madde 48's spot/perpetual/MAX EXPOSURE nuances are deliberately
//      postponed until real setups/positions exist to test them against,
//      i.e. after the Veto Engine). Of Madde 18's five named archetypes
//      (PULLBACK CONTINUATION, BREAKOUT RETEST, RANGE REJECTION, FAILED
//      BREAKOUT REVERSAL, MEAN REVERSION), only BREAKOUT RETEST is
//      implemented — it reuses the Breakout FSM (Madde 20-21) as its ENTIRE
//      trigger/confirmation/invalidation/expiry machinery (Madde 111 — no
//      new state machine invented); the other four are declared in the
//      SetupType enum (documenting the full taxonomy) but have no detection
//      logic, so the classifier simply never outputs them. Eligibility
//      (Madde 19, REGIME COMPATIBILITY) is a pure function of breakoutDir
//      vs. primaryRegime — UP eligible in BULL_TREND/TRANSITION, DOWN
//      eligible in BEAR_TREND/TRANSITION, neither eligible in RANGE (Madde
//      19's own worked example pairs RANGE with rejection/mean-reversion,
//      not breakout continuation). This FINALLY wires the state machine
//      beyond DATA_INVALID/FLAT: FLAT -> WATCH (BREAKOUT_CANDIDATE) -> SETUP
//      (CONFIRMED_BREAKOUT) -> ENTRY_PENDING (RETEST_PENDING or ENTRY),
//      always gated by eligibility. At this point (v0.12.x) it was still
//      capped at ENTRY_PENDING pending the Veto Engine — see module 13.
//
//  13. VETO ENGINE (Madde 52-53) — per user decision, built next instead of
//      the remaining 4 setup archetypes, so the ALREADY-BUILT chain
//      (Regime -> Structure -> Zone -> Breakout FSM -> Setup Classifier ->
//      Risk Engine) could reach a real CONFIRMED_LONG/CONFIRMED_SHORT for
//      the first time, end-to-end, before breadth is added (the remaining
//      archetypes would otherwise stay stuck at ENTRY_PENDING just like
//      Risk Engine sat unused before the Setup Classifier existed). Runs
//      independently of score (Madde 52 — trivial, no scoring engine
//      exists). Implements only the HARD VETO / SOFT PENALTY categories
//      this script has real evidence for (Madde 139/140 — no fabricated
//      EXECUTION INVALID / LEVERAGE CASCADE / ACCOUNT CIRCUIT BREAKER /
//      position-exposure checks, none of which exist yet), in Madde 53's
//      precedence order: RISK INVALID (the live setup's Risk Engine status
//      != OK — reuses f_riskCalc, Madde 111), STRUCTURE INVALID (severe
//      MTF conflict, mtfAgreement == CONFLICT), SETUP INVALID (not
//      eligible or FSM failed/idle). SOFT PENALTIES (weak participation,
//      weak momentum, MTF NEUTRAL, low regime confidence, elevated
//      volatility) are informational only, never block CONFIRMED. Per
//      explicit user instruction: no new magic-number threshold is
//      hardcoded — R:R is already i_minRR (Risk Engine's own input), and
//      the one new threshold this module adds (the ENTRY_PENDING
//      veto-blocked timeout, Madde 55 v3.1.1 EK, previously an explicitly
//      open question) is i_entryPendingMaxBars, a real input. A
//      hard-vetoed setup is NEVER silently hidden — it stays visible at
//      ENTRY_PENDING with the reason in the VETO row until the timeout
//      expires (then reverts to FLAT, same as a failed/stale breakout).
//      currentState can only ever hold one value, so CONFIRMED_LONG and
//      CONFIRMED_SHORT structurally cannot coexist on the same bar (Madde
//      51 v3.1.1 EK invariant, satisfied by construction, not by an
//      explicit check). This is Phase F's most consequential module so
//      far: the engine can now, for the very first time, reach a real
//      CONFIRMED_LONG/CONFIRMED_SHORT rather than capping at ENTRY_PENDING.
//
// EXPLICITLY DEFERRED (not yet built — no silent/fake behavior, Madde 139/140):
//   - Full REACTION QUALITY per touch (needs Price Action + Participation
//     evidence — both now exist, but no scoring engine combines them yet,
//     Madde 41) and HTF_IMPORTANCE (needs the full MTF cascade, not just the
//     single-HTF module built this turn) are NOT computed — Zone exposes
//     freshness/touch-count/EMA-confluence only, not a fabricated single
//     "quality score". Same restraint applies to the Breakout FSM's
//     displacement/retest checks (Structure-family only).
//   - Regime Confidence's "structure agreement" factor (Madde 11) still NOT
//     wired up, same as before — deferred to its own reviewable step.
//   - Full Evidence Family aggregation / family caps (Madde 42) — deferred
//     until scoring/normalization (Madde 41) exists.
//   - Relative Strength — explicitly SKIPPED by user decision (see Phase E
//     note above), not merely postponed. Full multi-level MTF cascade (only
//     ONE HTF level is requested so far, not the full 1D/4H/1H/15m stack)
//     remains deferred.
//   - Compact panel (Madde 114), Alert engine (Madde 116-117). Four of the
//     five Setup Classifier archetypes (PULLBACK CONTINUATION, RANGE
//     REJECTION, FAILED BREAKOUT REVERSAL, MEAN REVERSION — only BREAKOUT
//     RETEST is detected so far; per user decision, deliberately deferred
//     until the Veto Engine existed so they can all be integrated against
//     it in one pass instead of piecemeal). Trigger engine (distinct from
//     the Setup Classifier's own trigger concept — Madde 64's broader
//     trigger taxonomy). Final Decision Engine (Madde 37) — the Veto
//     Engine now gates CONFIRMED_LONG/CONFIRMED_SHORT directly, but a
//     dedicated scoring/aggregation Decision Engine layer on top of it
//     does not exist yet. IN_POSITION/EXIT/COOLDOWN (Madde 55-56 Position
//     Lifecycle) still do not exist — need the Execution Engine, Phase G.
//     Position sizing beyond the Risk Engine's own diagnostic numbers
//     (Madde 48's spot/perpetual/MAX EXPOSURE nuances, Madde 88
//     backtest-time sizing) is out of scope until real positions exist to
//     test it against. Some Madde 52 hard-veto/soft-penalty candidates are
//     NOT checked because no data source exists for them yet: EXECUTION
//     INVALID, LEVERAGE CASCADE RISK (EK-A), ACCOUNT CIRCUIT BREAKER
//     (EK-C), position/exposure violation, unsupported timeframe (Madde
//     32), "late entry" (no defined threshold), repaint-sensitive final
//     signal (N/A — nothing here repaints), critical calculation
//     unavailable (already covered by Risk Engine's own NO STRUCTURAL
//     STOP/NO TARGET ZONE statuses, not duplicated). Phase C, D, AND E are
//     complete; Phase F is in progress (Risk Engine + Setup Classifier's
//     first archetype + Veto Engine done — the engine can now reach a
//     real CONFIRMED_LONG/CONFIRMED_SHORT) per the Madde 121 roadmap.
//
// Non-repaint policy unchanged (Madde 33-34): all diagnostics are computed
// live every tick (clearly marked), but `currentState`, `primaryRegime`,
// `barsInRegime`, Structure state, Zone state, and the Breakout FSM only ever
// advance on barstate.isconfirmed. ta.* functions (pivots, crossover/
// crossunder) are called unconditionally every bar; only the resulting STATE
// UPDATE is gated. Fibonacci levels are pure derivations of already-confirmed
// swing prices, so they carry the same non-repaint guarantee without needing
// their own gate.
//
// v0.4.1 QA FIX (🤍, Madde 125): RE10045 on bar 0 of a fresh chart —
// `array.get()` index out of bounds inside f_updateZones(). Root cause: Pine's
// `for i = a to b` does NOT skip when b < a — it still runs at least once
// (counting down), so on an empty array `to array.size(zones) - 1` (= -1)
// executed one iteration at index 0 against a zero-length array. Fixed by
// guarding every such loop (f_upsertZone, f_updateZones, f_nearestZone, and
// the three zone/box-drawing loops) with an explicit `array.size(...) > 0`
// check before entering the `for`.
//
// v0.9.1 QA FIX (🤍, Madde 125): CE10173 compile error — "Cannot assign a
// value of the 'simple na' type to the 'lastPriceAboveVwap' variable. The
// variable is declared with the 'const bool' type." Root cause: a Pine v6
// bool-specific quirk — `var bool x = na` infers x as `const bool` (unlike
// `var float x = na` / `var int x = na`, which infer permissively), so the
// later `lastPriceAboveVwap := priceAboveVwap` (a runtime series bool) gets
// rejected as a series-into-const assignment. Fixed by casting the
// initializer explicitly: `var bool lastPriceAboveVwap = bool(na)`.
//
// v0.9.2 QA FIX (🤍, Madde 125): runtime error in Bar Replay only — "Error on
// bar 10084: The requested historical offset (330) is beyond the historical
// buffer's limit (329)." Root cause: Pine auto-detects how many bars of
// history to keep per series, but Bar Replay enforces this more strictly
// than normal chart execution, and a script this size (many ta.* calls with
// their own lookbacks — EMA200, ta.percentrank(,100), MACD(12,26,9), RSI,
// pivots, RVOL/VWAP SMAs — plus explicit `[]` offsets like
// open/close/rsiValue[i_pivotRight]) can need more auto-detected buffer than
// Pine allocates by default, especially under Replay's tighter limit. Fixed
// per Pine's own documented remedy for this exact error: explicitly reserve
// the buffer via `max_bars_back = 500` on the indicator() call, well above
// every lookback actually used in this script.
//
// v0.11.1 QA FIX (🤍, Madde 125): user caught (via screenshots) that RISK
// SHORT showed R:R 21-34 and status "OK" while price had ALREADY traded
// above the computed short stop. Root cause: when no un-broken opposing
// zone exists yet, the Risk Engine's stop reference falls back to
// lastSwingHighPrice/lastSwingLowPrice (Madde 14's central swing function) —
// but a swing is only "known" pivotRight bars after it actually happened,
// so during a strong breakout (confirmed BOS UP in this case) price can
// close well past that stale swing level before a NEW swing gets confirmed.
// f_riskCalc was applying the ATR buffer and computing R:R against that
// already-breached reference as if it were still valid, producing a
// mechanically inflated R:R (tiny stop distance vs. a distant target) on a
// premise that was already false. Fixed by checking, in f_riskCalc, whether
// `entry` has already crossed the RAW (un-buffered) stopRaw before doing
// anything else — if so, the status is now the explicit "ALREADY
// INVALIDATED" (R:R reported as N/A, not a fabricated number) instead of a
// false "OK". Highlighted in orange in the diagnostics table.
//
// v0.12.1 QA FIX (🤍, Madde 125): user caught STATE showing ENTRY_PENDING
// while the SETUP row showed NONE at the same time. Root cause: setupType
// reused f_isIdleBreakoutState (built for the Breakout FSM's own "can a NEW
// candidate start here" question) to decide "is there a setup to report" —
// the two questions disagree exactly at BreakoutFSMState.ENTRY (idle for a
// fresh candidate, but still the live result the state machine correctly
// keeps at ENTRY_PENDING). Fixed with a DEDICATED f_isActiveSetupState
// function for the Setup Classifier's own question (BREAKOUT_CANDIDATE/
// CONFIRMED_BREAKOUT/RETEST_PENDING/ENTRY = active); f_isIdleBreakoutState
// itself was left untouched since it is correct for its own purpose.
// =============================================================================

// Title/shorttitle kept short and FIXED on purpose (TradingView hard limits:
// title <=128 chars, shorttitle much shorter) — a v0.5 title that spelled out
// every module by name already broke the 128-char limit once modules kept
// being added. Full module list lives in the header comment above and in
// ENGINE_VERSION instead, where there is no length limit.
indicator("BTC PRO ANALYSIS ENGINE", shorttitle = "BTC-PRO", overlay = true, max_labels_count = 200, max_boxes_count = 50, max_lines_count = 50, max_bars_back = 500)

var string ENGINE_VERSION = "v0.13.0-phaseF-veto-engine"

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// STATE MACHINE SKELETON (Madde 55)
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
enum EngineState
    DATA_INVALID
    FLAT
    WATCH
    SETUP
    ENTRY_PENDING
    CONFIRMED_LONG
    CONFIRMED_SHORT
    IN_POSITION
    EXIT
    COOLDOWN

f_stateLabel(EngineState s) =>
    switch s
        EngineState.DATA_INVALID   => "DATA_INVALID"
        EngineState.FLAT           => "FLAT"
        EngineState.WATCH          => "WATCH"
        EngineState.SETUP          => "SETUP"
        EngineState.ENTRY_PENDING  => "ENTRY_PENDING"
        EngineState.CONFIRMED_LONG => "CONFIRMED_LONG"
        EngineState.CONFIRMED_SHORT => "CONFIRMED_SHORT"
        EngineState.IN_POSITION    => "IN_POSITION"
        EngineState.EXIT           => "EXIT"
        EngineState.COOLDOWN       => "COOLDOWN"
        =>                             "UNKNOWN"

// STATE row coloring (diagnostics table): DATA_INVALID=red,
// CONFIRMED_LONG=lime, CONFIRMED_SHORT=red, FLAT=gray, everything else
// (WATCH/SETUP/ENTRY_PENDING — "something is in progress") = yellow.
f_stateColor(EngineState s) =>
    s == EngineState.DATA_INVALID    ? color.red :
     s == EngineState.CONFIRMED_LONG  ? color.lime :
     s == EngineState.CONFIRMED_SHORT ? color.red :
     s == EngineState.FLAT            ? color.gray :
     color.yellow

var EngineState currentState = EngineState.DATA_INVALID

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// EVIDENCE FAMILY TAXONOMY (Madde 5) — documentation-only at this stage.
// No scoring/aggregation engine exists yet; this enum exists so each module's
// output can be explicitly tagged with the family it belongs to as it is
// built, instead of retrofitting the taxonomy later.
// Producers so far: CONTEXT_REGIME + VOLATILITY (Market Regime), STRUCTURE
// (also standing in for "Dow" per Madde 61 — the Breakout FSM uses this same
// family too, since it only reasons about price vs. a structural level),
// LOCATION (Zone module AND Fibonacci module both — Madde 4 names the
// combined hierarchy stage "LOCATION / ZONE"; Madde 17 explicitly calls
// Fibonacci "location evidence", so it shares the SAME family as Zone rather
// than getting its own), TRIGGER (Price Action module — Madde 64 lists
// "rejection"/"reclaim"/"close confirmation" as trigger examples, which is
// exactly what Price Action's patterns are), MOMENTUM (RSI + MACD histogram
// only, not also Stochastic/CCI, to avoid double-counting within this same
// family, Madde 6), PARTICIPATION (this module — RVOL + OBV alignment only,
// same double-counting reasoning applied to volume-flavored indicators).
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
enum EvidenceFamily
    CONTEXT_REGIME
    DIRECTION
    STRUCTURE
    LOCATION
    TRIGGER
    PARTICIPATION
    MOMENTUM
    VOLATILITY
    MTF
    RISK
    EXECUTION

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// MARKET REGIME ENUMS (Madde 9)
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
enum RegimeType
    BULL_TREND
    BEAR_TREND
    RANGE
    TRANSITION

enum VolRegime
    LOW_VOL
    NORMAL_VOL
    HIGH_VOL
    EXTREME_VOL

enum ConfidenceLevel
    LOW
    MEDIUM
    HIGH

f_regimeLabel(RegimeType r) =>
    switch r
        RegimeType.BULL_TREND => "BULL_TREND"
        RegimeType.BEAR_TREND => "BEAR_TREND"
        RegimeType.RANGE      => "RANGE"
        RegimeType.TRANSITION => "TRANSITION"
        =>                        "UNKNOWN"

f_volLabel(VolRegime v) =>
    switch v
        VolRegime.LOW_VOL     => "LOW_VOL"
        VolRegime.NORMAL_VOL  => "NORMAL_VOL"
        VolRegime.HIGH_VOL    => "HIGH_VOL"
        VolRegime.EXTREME_VOL => "EXTREME_VOL"
        =>                        "UNKNOWN"

f_confLabel(ConfidenceLevel c) =>
    switch c
        ConfidenceLevel.LOW    => "LOW"
        ConfidenceLevel.MEDIUM => "MEDIUM"
        ConfidenceLevel.HIGH   => "HIGH"
        =>                         "UNKNOWN"

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// MARKET STRUCTURE ENUMS (Madde 14, 61)
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
enum SwingLabel
    NONE
    HH
    LH
    HL
    LL

enum StructureBias
    NEUTRAL
    BULLISH
    BEARISH

enum StructureEvent
    NONE
    BOS_UP
    BOS_DOWN
    CHOCH_UP
    CHOCH_DOWN

f_swingLabel(SwingLabel s) =>
    switch s
        SwingLabel.HH => "HH"
        SwingLabel.LH => "LH"
        SwingLabel.HL => "HL"
        SwingLabel.LL => "LL"
        =>                "N/A"

f_biasLabel(StructureBias b) =>
    switch b
        StructureBias.BULLISH => "BULLISH"
        StructureBias.BEARISH => "BEARISH"
        =>                        "NEUTRAL"

f_structEventLabel(StructureEvent e) =>
    switch e
        StructureEvent.BOS_UP    => "BOS UP"
        StructureEvent.BOS_DOWN  => "BOS DOWN"
        StructureEvent.CHOCH_UP  => "CHoCH UP"
        StructureEvent.CHOCH_DOWN => "CHoCH DOWN"
        =>                            "NONE"

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// BREAKOUT / RETEST STATE MACHINE ENUMS (Madde 20-21)
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
enum BreakoutDirection
    NONE
    UP
    DOWN

enum BreakoutFSMState
    PRE_BREAKOUT
    BREAKOUT_CANDIDATE
    CONFIRMED_BREAKOUT
    RETEST_PENDING
    ENTRY
    FAILED_BREAKOUT
    REVERSAL_CANDIDATE
    STALE

f_breakoutDirLabel(BreakoutDirection d) =>
    switch d
        BreakoutDirection.UP   => "UP"
        BreakoutDirection.DOWN => "DOWN"
        =>                         "NONE"

f_breakoutStateLabel(BreakoutFSMState s) =>
    switch s
        BreakoutFSMState.PRE_BREAKOUT       => "PRE_BREAKOUT"
        BreakoutFSMState.BREAKOUT_CANDIDATE => "BREAKOUT_CANDIDATE"
        BreakoutFSMState.CONFIRMED_BREAKOUT => "CONFIRMED_BREAKOUT"
        BreakoutFSMState.RETEST_PENDING     => "RETEST_PENDING"
        BreakoutFSMState.ENTRY              => "ENTRY (structural only)"
        BreakoutFSMState.FAILED_BREAKOUT    => "FAILED_BREAKOUT"
        BreakoutFSMState.REVERSAL_CANDIDATE => "REVERSAL_CANDIDATE"
        BreakoutFSMState.STALE              => "STALE"
        =>                                      "UNKNOWN"

// Idle = a fresh BREAKOUT_CANDIDATE may start from here (Madde 20). Pure
// function, no outer-scope references, safe to define this early.
f_isIdleBreakoutState(BreakoutFSMState s) =>
    s == BreakoutFSMState.PRE_BREAKOUT or s == BreakoutFSMState.STALE or
     s == BreakoutFSMState.FAILED_BREAKOUT or s == BreakoutFSMState.REVERSAL_CANDIDATE or
     s == BreakoutFSMState.ENTRY

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// SETUP CLASSIFIER ENUMS (Madde 18) — all FIVE archetypes Madde 18 names are
// declared here (documenting the full taxonomy, same pattern as
// EvidenceFamily/RegimeType existing before every producer was built), but
// only BREAKOUT_RETEST has detection logic wired up this turn — see the
// SETUP CLASSIFIER computation section for why (it reuses the Breakout FSM
// almost entirely). The other four are declared, unused, and will simply
// never be output — not a fake placeholder (Madde 139/140).
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
enum SetupType
    NONE
    BREAKOUT_RETEST
    PULLBACK_CONTINUATION
    RANGE_REJECTION
    FAILED_BREAKOUT_REVERSAL
    MEAN_REVERSION

f_setupTypeLabel(SetupType t) =>
    switch t
        SetupType.BREAKOUT_RETEST          => "BREAKOUT RETEST"
        SetupType.PULLBACK_CONTINUATION    => "PULLBACK CONTINUATION"
        SetupType.RANGE_REJECTION          => "RANGE REJECTION"
        SetupType.FAILED_BREAKOUT_REVERSAL => "FAILED BREAKOUT REVERSAL"
        SetupType.MEAN_REVERSION           => "MEAN REVERSION"
        =>                                     "NONE"

// Madde 19 — SETUP ELIGIBILITY GATE / REGIME COMPATIBILITY: a breakout-retest
// continuation is only eligible when its direction does not fight the
// current regime. Pure function (no outer-scope references), so it stays
// safe to define this early next to the other Breakout FSM helpers.
// regimeConfidence is deliberately NOT part of this check — that is a
// separate, already-documented gate (Madde 11/37) reserved for the future
// Decision Engine, not to be conflated with regime-TYPE compatibility
// (Madde 111: don't double up two different gates into one).
f_breakoutRetestEligible(BreakoutDirection dir, RegimeType regime) =>
    dir == BreakoutDirection.UP   ? (regime == RegimeType.BULL_TREND or regime == RegimeType.TRANSITION) :
     dir == BreakoutDirection.DOWN ? (regime == RegimeType.BEAR_TREND or regime == RegimeType.TRANSITION) :
     false

// v0.12.1 QA FIX (🤍, Madde 125): "is there a setup to REPORT right now" is
// NOT the same question as f_isIdleBreakoutState's "can a NEW candidate
// START from here" — they disagree exactly at BreakoutFSMState.ENTRY (idle
// for starting a fresh candidate, but still the live result of the setup
// that just completed, which the state machine correctly keeps at
// ENTRY_PENDING). Reusing f_isIdleBreakoutState for setupType caused the
// STATE row to show ENTRY_PENDING while the SETUP row showed NONE — a real
// inconsistency the user caught. A DEDICATED function for the Setup
// Classifier's own question, leaving f_isIdleBreakoutState untouched (it is
// correct for the Breakout FSM's own purpose).
f_isActiveSetupState(BreakoutFSMState s) =>
    s == BreakoutFSMState.BREAKOUT_CANDIDATE or s == BreakoutFSMState.CONFIRMED_BREAKOUT or
     s == BreakoutFSMState.RETEST_PENDING or s == BreakoutFSMState.ENTRY

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// MOMENTUM ENUMS (Madde 23) — a STATE label, never "RSI 30 = LONG" style
// automatic direction-from-level logic.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
enum MomentumState
    NEUTRAL
    ACCELERATING
    DECELERATING
    RECOVERING
    WEAKENING

enum MomentumDirection
    NONE
    BULLISH
    BEARISH

enum DivergenceType
    NONE
    BULLISH
    BEARISH

f_momStateLabel(MomentumState s) =>
    switch s
        MomentumState.ACCELERATING => "ACCELERATING"
        MomentumState.DECELERATING => "DECELERATING"
        MomentumState.RECOVERING   => "RECOVERING"
        MomentumState.WEAKENING    => "WEAKENING"
        =>                             "NEUTRAL"

f_momDirLabel(MomentumDirection d) =>
    switch d
        MomentumDirection.BULLISH => "BULLISH"
        MomentumDirection.BEARISH => "BEARISH"
        =>                            "NONE"

f_divergenceLabel(DivergenceType d) =>
    switch d
        DivergenceType.BULLISH => "BULLISH DIVERGENCE"
        DivergenceType.BEARISH => "BEARISH DIVERGENCE"
        =>                          "NONE"

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// PARTICIPATION ENUMS (Madde 24)
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
enum ParticipationState
    NORMAL
    EXPANDING
    CONTRACTING
    CONFIRMING
    DIVERGING

enum ParticipationDirection
    NONE
    BULLISH
    BEARISH

f_partStateLabel(ParticipationState s) =>
    switch s
        ParticipationState.EXPANDING   => "EXPANDING"
        ParticipationState.CONTRACTING => "CONTRACTING"
        ParticipationState.CONFIRMING  => "CONFIRMING"
        ParticipationState.DIVERGING   => "DIVERGING"
        =>                                 "NORMAL"

f_partDirLabel(ParticipationDirection d) =>
    switch d
        ParticipationDirection.BULLISH => "BULLISH"
        ParticipationDirection.BEARISH => "BEARISH"
        =>                                 "NONE"

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// MTF ENUMS (Madde 28-32) — HTF bias reuses StructureBias (same three values,
// same meaning: BULLISH/BEARISH/NEUTRAL direction read), not a duplicate
// near-identical enum (Madde 111). MtfAgreement is the NEW concept: how the
// HTF bias relates to the chart's own structureBias.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
enum MtfAgreement
    UNAVAILABLE
    AGREE
    CONFLICT
    NEUTRAL

f_mtfAgreementLabel(MtfAgreement a) =>
    switch a
        MtfAgreement.AGREE    => "AGREE"
        MtfAgreement.CONFLICT => "CONFLICT"
        MtfAgreement.NEUTRAL  => "NEUTRAL"
        =>                         "UNAVAILABLE"

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// SUPPORT/RESISTANCE ZONE TYPE + HELPERS (Madde 15, 16) — built ONLY on top of
// the central confirmed-swing function; no separate pivot logic here. All
// helpers take their thresholds as explicit parameters (never read inputs or
// later-declared globals directly) so they stay safe to define this early.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
type Zone
    float zoneHigh
    float zoneLow
    int   createdBar    // SWING_TIME of the swing that created/last extended it
    int   knownBar      // KNOWN_TIME the zone (or its last merge) became known
    int   lastTouchBar
    int   touchCount
    bool  broken
    int   brokenBar

f_upsertZone(array<Zone> zones, float zHigh, float zLow, int swingBar, int knownBar, float atrVal, float clusterMult, int maxZones) =>
    float newCenter = (zHigh + zLow) / 2
    int mergedIndex = -1
    // Pine's `for a to b` runs at least once even when b < a (it counts DOWN
    // in that case) — an empty array (size 0) makes `to array.size(zones)-1`
    // evaluate to -1, which without this guard still executes one iteration
    // at index 0 and crashes array.get() on bar 0. Always guard size > 0.
    if atrVal > 0 and array.size(zones) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(zones) - 1
            Zone z = array.get(zones, i)
            if not z.broken
                float zCenter = (z.zoneHigh + z.zoneLow) / 2
                if math.abs(newCenter - zCenter) <= atrVal * clusterMult
                    mergedIndex := i
                    break
    if mergedIndex >= 0
        Zone existing = array.get(zones, mergedIndex)
        existing.zoneHigh := math.max(existing.zoneHigh, zHigh)
        existing.zoneLow  := math.min(existing.zoneLow, zLow)
        existing.touchCount := existing.touchCount + 1
        existing.lastTouchBar := knownBar
    else
        Zone newZone = Zone.new(zoneHigh = zHigh, zoneLow = zLow, createdBar = swingBar, knownBar = knownBar, lastTouchBar = knownBar, touchCount = 1, broken = false, brokenBar = na)
        array.push(zones, newZone)
        if array.size(zones) > maxZones
            array.remove(zones, 0)
    true

f_updateZones(array<Zone> zones, bool isResistance, float barHigh, float barLow, float barClose, int curBar) =>
    // Same empty-array guard as f_upsertZone — see comment there.
    if array.size(zones) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(zones) - 1
            Zone z = array.get(zones, i)
            if not z.broken
                bool touched = barHigh >= z.zoneLow and barLow <= z.zoneHigh
                if touched and z.lastTouchBar != curBar
                    z.touchCount := z.touchCount + 1
                    z.lastTouchBar := curBar
                if isResistance and barClose > z.zoneHigh
                    z.broken := true
                    z.brokenBar := curBar
                if not isResistance and barClose < z.zoneLow
                    z.broken := true
                    z.brokenBar := curBar
    true

f_nearestZone(array<Zone> zones, float refPrice) =>
    float bestDist = na
    int bestIdx = -1
    if array.size(zones) > 0
        for i = 0 to array.size(zones) - 1
            Zone z = array.get(zones, i)
            if not z.broken
                float center = (z.zoneHigh + z.zoneLow) / 2
                float dist = math.abs(refPrice - center)
                if na(bestDist) or dist < bestDist
                    bestDist := dist
                    bestIdx := i
    bestIdx

f_zoneFreshness(Zone z, int curBar, int freshAgeBars, int staleAgeBars, int exhaustTouches) =>
    age = curBar - z.createdBar
    z.touchCount >= exhaustTouches ? "EXHAUSTED" : age > staleAgeBars ? "STALE" : age <= freshAgeBars ? "FRESH" : "AGING"

f_emaConfluence(Zone z, float ef, float em, float es, float atrVal, float mult) =>
    float lo = z.zoneLow - atrVal * mult
    float hi = z.zoneHigh + atrVal * mult
    (ef >= lo and ef <= hi) or (em >= lo and em <= hi) or (es >= lo and es <= hi)

f_zoneSummary(array<Zone> zones, int idx, float ef, float em, float es, float atrVal, float confMult, int curBar, int freshAge, int staleAge, int exhaustN) =>
    string result = "NONE"
    if idx >= 0
        Zone z = array.get(zones, idx)
        string fresh = f_zoneFreshness(z, curBar, freshAge, staleAge, exhaustN)
        bool conf = f_emaConfluence(z, ef, em, es, atrVal, confMult)
        result := fresh + "  " + str.tostring(z.zoneLow) + "-" + str.tostring(z.zoneHigh) + " (" + str.tostring(z.touchCount) + "x)" + (conf ? " EMA" : "")
    result

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// FIBONACCI HELPERS (Madde 17) — computed only from the two most recently
// confirmed structural swings (the central swing function above), never a
// random last-N-bars high/low. Pure functions, no outer-scope references.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
f_fibLevel(bool legUp, float hi, float lo, float ratio) =>
    legUp ? hi - (hi - lo) * ratio : lo + (hi - lo) * ratio

f_fibTouchLabel(float price, float f236, float f382, float f500, float f618, float f786, float tol) =>
    string result = "NONE"
    if not na(f236) and math.abs(price - f236) <= tol
        result := "0.236"
    if not na(f382) and math.abs(price - f382) <= tol
        result := "0.382"
    if not na(f500) and math.abs(price - f500) <= tol
        result := "0.5"
    if not na(f618) and math.abs(price - f618) <= tol
        result := "0.618"
    if not na(f786) and math.abs(price - f786) <= tol
        result := "0.786"
    result

f_drawFibLevel(array<line> lines, array<label> labels, int startBar, int endBar, float level, string txt, color col) =>
    if not na(level)
        ln = line.new(startBar, level, endBar, level, color = col, style = line.style_dashed)
        array.push(lines, ln)
        lb = label.new(endBar, level, txt, style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(col, 100), textcolor = col, size = size.tiny)
        array.push(labels, lb)
    true

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// RISK ENGINE HELPERS (Madde 44-49) — pure functions, no outer-scope
// references, so they work identically for the LONG and SHORT structural
// ideas below (Madde 50 long/short symmetry). `stopRaw`/`targetRaw` are the
// UN-buffered structural levels (nearest opposing zone edge or last swing);
// this function applies the ATR buffer and the stop-distance/R:R gates.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
f_riskCalc(bool isLong, float entry, float stopRaw, float targetRaw, float atrVal, float atrBufferMult, float maxStopPct, float minRR) =>
    // v0.11.1 QA FIX: `stopRaw` is the RAW structural reference (a fallback
    // last-swing price can be stale — the swing itself is only "known"
    // pivotRight bars after the fact, Madde 14, while price may have
    // already closed beyond it with a confirmed BOS). If entry has ALREADY
    // crossed past stopRaw, the structural condition that would justify
    // this LONG/SHORT idea is already gone — reporting a "stop"/R:R past
    // that point would be evidence built on an already-broken premise
    // (Madde 139/140: never a fabricated result). Checked on the
    // UN-buffered stopRaw (the real structural line; the ATR buffer is
    // only noise padding on top of it, Madde 44).
    bool alreadyBreached = not na(stopRaw) and (isLong ? entry <= stopRaw : entry >= stopRaw)
    float stopLevel = na(stopRaw) or na(atrVal) ? na : (isLong ? stopRaw - atrVal * atrBufferMult : stopRaw + atrVal * atrBufferMult)
    float stopDist = na(stopLevel) ? na : math.abs(entry - stopLevel)
    bool stopTooWide = not na(stopDist) and entry > 0 and stopDist > entry * maxStopPct / 100
    float rewardDist = na(targetRaw) ? na : math.abs(targetRaw - entry)
    float rr = (alreadyBreached or na(stopDist) or stopDist <= 0 or na(rewardDist)) ? na : rewardDist / stopDist
    bool rrOk = not na(rr) and rr >= minRR
    string status = na(stopLevel) ? "NO STRUCTURAL STOP" :
         alreadyBreached ? "ALREADY INVALIDATED" :
         na(targetRaw) ? "NO TARGET ZONE" :
         stopTooWide ? "STOP TOO WIDE" :
         not rrOk ? "R:R BELOW MIN" :
         "OK"
    [stopLevel, targetRaw, stopDist, rewardDist, rr, status]

// Madde 48: Risk Amount = Equity x Risk%, Position Size = Risk Amount / Stop
// Distance. Leverage only changes MARGIN required, never the risk-based
// position size itself (Madde 48: leverage never assumed without an
// explicit, user-set value — default 1.0 = spot/no leverage).
f_positionSize(float equity, float riskPct, float stopDist, float entry, float leverage) =>
    float riskAmount = equity * riskPct / 100
    float posSize = (na(stopDist) or stopDist <= 0) ? na : riskAmount / stopDist
    float notional = na(posSize) ? na : posSize * entry
    float margin = na(notional) or leverage <= 0 ? na : notional / leverage
    [riskAmount, posSize, notional, margin]

f_riskLine(float stopLevel, float targetLevel, float rr, string status) =>
    "stop " + (na(stopLevel) ? "N/A" : str.tostring(stopLevel)) +
     "  target " + (na(targetLevel) ? "N/A" : str.tostring(targetLevel)) +
     "  R:R " + (na(rr) ? "N/A" : str.tostring(rr, "#.##")) +
     "  " + status

f_posSizeLine(float posSize, float notional, float margin) =>
    na(posSize) ? "N/A" : str.tostring(posSize, "#.####") + " BTC  ($" + str.tostring(notional, "#.##") + " notional, $" + str.tostring(margin, "#.##") + " margin)"

